From ae412c89d63b50e50f75ae3bf1b7fa346abec8e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:28:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stiffness matrices on a device: products K B computed once
 per group of five blocks, positions of the entries used

- One thread per node b of an element and per group of five nodes a: the
  products of the tangent operator by the operator B of the node b, which
  take most of the operations, are computed once for the five blocks (a, b)
  instead of once per block. The operations on each block are made in the
  same order.
- Loops over the tables of the non-zero entries of B and over the
  components of the unknowns fully unrolled (MFEM_MGIS_UNROLL, CUDA and
  HIP): nvcc 13.0 no longer unrolled them, and read the entries from the
  constant memory at each iteration.
- The positions of the entries in the rows of the matrix are also computed
  and read on a device: the measurement which had excluded them was made in
  double precision on a GPU with few double precision units, where the
  kernel is bound by these units.
- Quadratic tetrahedra in finite strain, 196,608 elements, RTX 5080, single
  precision: assembly 15.5 ms before, 7.1 ms without positions and 4.7 ms
  with them; ordered assembly 20.3 ms before, 10.4 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
